Make aquamarine's nested Wayland backend work under a headless wlroots host.

Three changes to src/backend/Wayland.cpp:

1. Flush the output's initial commit as soon as the output is created. Without
   this the commit sits in the client buffer until the host sends an event, and
   a headless host with no input devices never sends one, so no monitor appears.

2. Apply the toplevel size only after the xdg_surface configure has been acked.
   Emitting the state from the toplevel configure handler makes Hyprland commit
   a buffer before the ack, which wlroots hosts reject with
   "xdg_surface has never been configured".

3. Bind wl_seat, xdg_wm_base and wl_compositor at the version the host offers
   when that is lower than the one asked for. Older hosts (labwc 0.7 on
   Ubuntu 24.04, for example) otherwise end the connection with
   "invalid version for global".

Written against aquamarine 0.15.1; also applies to 0.14.0.

--- a/src/backend/Wayland.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/Wayland.cpp
@@ -118,15 +118,15 @@
 
